<Project>

  <!-- The board table: one row per target name, spelled maker-product.
       A row names the processor class, the payload map, the prebuilt
       kernel, the runtime archive set, the build-attributes donor, the
       tier objects the image links in the link's order (the shim's five
       link objects, the P/Invoke-facing surface object, the GPIO API
       object, the bus and PWM device objects, the serial device object
       and the serial layer's object, the three collector row objects,
       the C-library closure),
       the row's own objects among them (BoardObjects: its shim core and
       system-call objects and its heap and collect rows, four names from
       the Objects list, which ride in the row's board package where the
       rest ride in the processor class's runtime package; the link keeps
       the Objects order and takes each from the package that carries it),
       the thread stack facts (the kernel's stack pool for the row, the
       default managed stack and its clamp, and the bytes of the pool the
       kernel's own threads hold on the row's kernels (StackKernel: the
       idle thread's stack and the stack of the thread that runs a hosted
       program's Main; the SDK computes the thread pool's most workers
       from it), in bytes: copies of the kernel's and the hosting layer's
       constants that the verification chain checks against the
       sources), the emulator machine (empty
       for a physical board), the image base, and the two streams' default
       channels with the row's legal channel set (LogChannel, ConsoleChannel,
       Channels: copies of the facts file's channels row, which the chain
       checks too). A row that carries an
       external RAM range names beside its default kernel (init at boot)
       the two archives built for the lazy init modes, which the project's
       RhuExternalRamInit value picks; the other rows carry none. Such a
       row also names a second payload map (MapInternal), which keeps the
       hosted runtime's rehydrated type data and the managed heap's window
       in the chip's own RAM, picked by the project's RhuManagedMemory
       value in place of the row's map. A row whose board carries a
       memory-mapped external flash names a third payload map
       (MapExternalFlash), which places the hosted program's managed code,
       read-only data and unwind tables in that flash, executed in place,
       picked by the project's RhuProgramMemory value; such a row may say
       which home a project that names none gets (ProgramMemoryDefault:
       external; a row without the attribute keeps the chip's own flash).
       A row whose board has a network the kernel serves names two kernel
       sets: its kernels (Kernel and the two lazy archives) are built with
       the network, and a second set (KernelNoNetwork,
       KernelNoNetworkRamInitFirstUse, KernelNoNetworkRamInitBackground,
       under the row's folder no-network) is built without it, picked by
       the project's network knob (Sdk.props names it) and wherever
       RhuManagedMemory is internal; a row with one kernel names no second
       set, and the table
       does not say whether that kernel carries a network. A row whose board package
       carries a flash region names it (FlashRegions: the packed file of
       a fixed place in the board's flash outside the program, such as a
       radio's firmware, with its record and its notices beside it in
       the package; a flash tool writes it at a deploy, and the SDK puts
       it beside the image); a row without the attribute has none. A row
       whose chip serves a low-power UART names those blocks
       (UartLowPowerBlocks: a number whose bit n is set for UART block n;
       the hosting layer names such a block's device file /dev/ttyLP<n>
       and every other block's /dev/ttyS<n>, and the board's facts file
       states the same kind for the row's port); a row without the
       attribute has no such block. A row says where the
       library the standard analog classes express a voltage in fits
       (AnalogVoltageFits): internal-flash when the chip's own flash holds
       it, external-flash when the board's external flash alone does; a
       row without the attribute does not hold it, and the SDK leaves the
       analog voltage switch false there. A row says when its board
       requires the code optimization (RequiresOptimization): the board's
       memory does not hold the board class's program with the framework's
       code compiled without it (measured: that image does not link under
       the row's map), so an image compiled without the optimization as a
       whole is refused at the link for the row, in words that say what the
       board's memory requires; the SDK compiles the framework's code with
       the optimization on for every row, and a Debug configuration leaves
       only the program's own code unoptimized. The measure is of a program
       in the chip's own flash: placed in the row's external flash
       (RhuProgramMemory=external) the image compiled without the
       optimization as a whole links, and the attribute is not read. Every
       path is relative to the root of the package that carries it. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <LamellaTargetBoardRow Include="arm-mps2-an500"
                 Class="cortex-m7"
                 Map="maps/payload-mps2-an500.x"
                 MapInternal="maps/payload-mps2-an500-internal.x"
                 Kernel="kernels/arm-mps2-an500/librhu_kernel.a"
                 KernelRamInitFirstUse="kernels/arm-mps2-an500/ram-init-first-use/librhu_kernel.a"
                 KernelRamInitBackground="kernels/arm-mps2-an500/ram-init-background/librhu_kernel.a"
                 Archives="archives/cortex-m7"
                 Donor="tier/cortex-m7/attr-donor-v7em.bin"
                 Objects="tier/cortex-m7/shim-core.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-sysnative.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-libc-glue.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-stdio-sym.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-host.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-pal-surface.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-sockaddr.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-socket.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-netinfo.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-gpiod.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-busdev.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-pwmfs.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-iiofs.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-ttydev.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-ports-native.o tier/cortex-m7/skel-row.o tier/cortex-m7/heap-row.o tier/cortex-m7/collect-row.o tier/cortex-m7/rt-libc.o"
                 BoardObjects="tier/cortex-m7/shim-core.o tier/cortex-m7/shim-sysnative.o tier/cortex-m7/heap-row.o tier/cortex-m7/collect-row.o"
                 StackPool="131072"
                 StackDefault="16384"
                 StackClamp="24576"
                 StackKernel="17408"
                 LogChannel="uart0"
                 ConsoleChannel="uart0"
                 Channels="uart0 uart1 memory off"
                 Machine="mps2-an500"
                 Base="0x00000000" />
